{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:08:03.249Z","data":{"text":"Task 6 is complete.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **`src/core/report/query-pauses.ts`** (new): exports `PAUSE_TABLES` (`pauses(change, task, paused_at, until, source)`) and `insertPauses`, modelled on `TASK_STREAM_TABLES`/`insertTaskStreamTables`. It lists each archived change's digit-named task streams in numeric order, reads them with `readEventStream`, and inserts one row per `paused` event — `task`/`until`/`source` from the object `data`, `paused_at` the event's `timestamp`, wrong-typed fields as null.\n\n2. **`src/core/report/query-tables.ts`**: added `...PAUSE_TABLES` after `...TASK_OUTCOME_TABLES` and calls `insertPauses` after `insertLinkFindings`.\n\n3. **Pinned table lists** in `tests/query-command.test.ts`, `tests/query-trial-tables.test.ts`, `tests/query-tables.test.ts`: the `pauses` line/entry added after `task_outcomes`.\n\n4. **`tests/query-task-outcomes.test.ts`**: the `task outcomes listed` case now asserts `task_outcomes` comes directly after `link_findings` instead of last — the earlier blocker, now in scope.\n\n5. **`tests/query-pauses.test.ts`** (new): proves all four scenarios through the real `osq query` command.\n\n**Verification:** the task verify passes 4/4, and the proposal's `pnpm verify` exits 0. No blockers remain."}}
